  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nThere's no preview at all for any urls from keytown.me, for example, neither title nor image. The issue title might be misleading, that's only an assumption.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- post an url like https://keytown.me/\r\n- no preview appears as if it's not even an url\r\n\r\nLog reads:\r\n\r\n```\r\n2018-02-20 09:48:09,012 - synapse.http.server - 124 - INFO - GET-6- <SynapseRequest at 0x7faf78407518 method=GET uri=/_matrix/media/r0/preview_url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fkeytown.me%2F&ts=1519109288279&access_token=<redacted> clientproto=HTTP/1.0 site=8008> SynapseError: 500 - Failed to download content: [<twisted.python.failure.Failure OpenSSL.SSL.Error: [('SSL routines', 'ssl3_read_bytes', 'sslv3 alert handshake failure')]>]\r\n```\r\nFrom what I found this happens if the site disabled SSLv3 on their end or if cipher suites don't match (see #2350). Some advice downgrading python-cryptography but it didn't help in my case.\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n<!-- IMPORTANT: please answer the following questions, to help us narrow down the problem -->\r\n\r\n- **Homeserver**: own homeserver\r\n- **Version**:  Synapse/0.26.0\r\n- **Install method**: package manager\r\n- **Platform**: set up on Debian 9.3 amd64.",
